  "verdict": "No full-video/general VLM judge tested achieves acceptable miss/false alarm rates for author-injected temporal gameplay anomalies. Best author accuracy 54.1pct, near chance balanced dataset. Qwen3-VL-8B 5 FPS TP2 FN748 FP0, an always-clean bias. Gemini3 Flash raw video TP654 FN96 FP650, an almost-everything-is-defective bias. Authors source tables independently rechecked. Metadata-only clip size/class classifier 56.6pct heldout on 320 separate source files, cannot be directly statistically compared to VLM on all1500.",
  "conditional_immediate_tool_selection": "Source/DOM geometry and exact approved timeline for hard known constraints; OCR/feature tracking/pHash as evidence and abstain where uncertain, no VLM automatic verdict. For engine temporal failures, require object-level state, pose and displacement continuity or debug instrumentation, distinguish world-state defects from full-frame stalls. Any VLM recommendation requires new source-engine, human clean/defective labels, calibrated per-type FN/FP, latency and work-group contention tests.",
  "limitations": [
    "Published author in-engine source glitch/normal truth is not blind independent subjective fault annotation; output cannot establish perceptual natural render stalls.",
    "Published models were run by authors, on four L40S for open-model family, not locally on Thor/Nitro; service versions, quantization, prompts and workloads differ.",
    "Only two Godot demo environments; clip variants correlate within source and scene, and published Table3 does not provide a heldout new rendering engine result.",
    "Some models obtain high recall simply by predicting nearly all videos glitchy; always-glitch untrained baseline F1 66.7pct on 1:1 class data.",
    "Higher sampling frame rate from 1 to 5 FPS does not consistently improve practical accuracy or model calibration; Gemini raw-video accuracy still near chance.",
    "The source metadata 320-file heldout split trained on other indices from the SAME source engine and categories, not untouched external game generators; source file size may encode duration, bitrate or scene content.",
    "Source frozen animation means CHARACTER POSE not updating while world video continues; FFmpeg whole-screen freezedetect cannot prove absence of this anomaly.",
    "Source original dataset videos ~60GB were deliberately not downloaded to avoid production resource contention and source media redistribution; quantitative VLM confusion is literature, not reproduced model inference.",
    "No event-level temporal IoU or defect timing ground truth extracted and no natural-visual-quality human MOS on new source provided."
  ]
}
